{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"487c438c-7338-4a3c-ab8e-dac7395e18b7","status":"SUCCESS","response":"Investigated the producer ([`catalog.build`](file:///workspace/catalog.py)) and consumer ([`query.get`](file:///workspace/query.py)):\n\n1. **Root Causes**:\n   - [`query.get`](file:///workspace/query.py) bypassed canonical normalization and used `name.lower()` instead of [`canonical.key`](file:///workspace/canonical.py), missing leading/trailing whitespace stripping.\n   - [`canonical.key`](file:///workspace/canonical.py) used `.lower()` instead of `.casefold()`, which does not perform full Unicode caseless matching (e.g. matching German `ß` and `SS`, or Greek uppercase/lowercase variants).\n\n2. **Changes Made**:\n   - Updated [`canonical.key`](file:///workspace/canonical.py) to use `value.strip().casefold()`, providing Unicode case-insensitive matching while stripping surrounding whitespace.\n   - Updated [`query.get`](file:///workspace/query.py) to import and use [`key`](file:///workspace/canonical.py) to query the catalog so both producer and consumer share identical canonical key semantics without changing the catalog's stored values.\n   - Added test coverage in [tests/test_query.py](file:///workspace/tests/test_query.py) covering Unicode casefold normalization and whitespace handling.\n","duration_seconds":47.626071354,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":156463,"output_tokens":1568,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":64759,"total_tokens":158031}}}
